msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-copy-log.md:16
msgid ""
"To copy the build log of the `hello` package from https://cache.nixos.org to "
"the local store:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-copy-log.md:19
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix store copy-log --from https://cache.nixos.org --eval-store auto "
"nixpkgs#hello\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-copy-log.md:23
msgid "You can verify that the log is available locally:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-copy-log.md:29
msgid ""
"(The flag `--substituters ''` avoids querying `https://cache.nixos.org` for "
"the log.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-copy-log.md:32
msgid ""
"To copy the log for a specific [store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-"
"store-derivation) via SSH:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-copy-log.md:36
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix store copy-log --to ssh-ng://machine /nix/store/"
"yaxvykk956vdrwrx9cxyw44mpqr1ml7i-glibc-2.33-59.drv\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-copy-log.md:40
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-copy-log.md:42
msgid ""
"`nix store copy-log` copies build logs between two Nix stores. The source "
"store is specified using `--from` and the destination using `--to`. If one "
"of these is omitted, it defaults to the local store."
msgstr ""

